
Free Domain Providers for Your Backup Server Cluster

When hosting a secondary backup node of the Archverse to distribute server load and map queries safely, you can connect an absolute free domain provider to your Nginx proxy.
The top free domain allocation layers available include:
• DuckDNS (duckdns.org): A completely free, non-expiring Dynamic DNS (DDNS) provider. It allows you to claim a free subdomain (e.g., archverse-backup.duckdns.org) and route it directly to any public VPS IP address. It natively supports free automated Let's Encrypt SSL script registration.
• No-IP (noip.com): Offers up to 3 free subdomains (e.g., archverse.ddns.net). Note: Free accounts require a brief manual click confirmation via email once every 30 days to stay active.
• FreeDNS (freedns.afraid.org): A massive public community domain registry offering thousands of free subdomains across various hosting extensions.

🛠️ Direct Backup DNS Configuration Map

Once you claim your free subdomain from DuckDNS, simply map it to your backup cloud server by issuing an update ping script task:
bash
curl -k "https://duckdns.org"
